    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Debussy and Miller: From Love to the Sea"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>This program highlights the viola’s deep, expressive voice in Canadian composer Cassandra Miller’s Concerto, a poignant reflection on separation premiered in 2023 by Lawrence Power. Meanwhile, Debussy paints a vivid portrait of the sea with impressionistic colours, immersing listeners in a nostalgic and dreamlike soundscape. Enjoy a musical journey that is both powerful and poetic.</p>\n<p>Coffee is offered courtesy of our Symphonic Matinees presenter, Chartwell, as soon as the doors open.</p>\n"
      }
    ]
  },
