    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.osm.ca/app/uploads/2026/03/payare-poulenc-sibelius-1080x1080-osm2627-ang.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.osm.ca/en/concert/payare-conducts-poulenc-and-sibelius/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g1543920"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.osm.ca/en/concert/payare-conducts-poulenc-and-sibelius/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Payare Conducts Poulenc and Sibelius"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>Two voices of modernity meet here: Poulenc and Sibelius—each firmly rooted in their time, yet deeply attuned to the legacy of the past. Poulenc’s Organ Concerto, brought to life by Jean-Willy Kunz with meditative intensity, blends baroque solemnity with flashes of 20th-century brilliance. That same fertile tension runs through Sibelius’s Symphony no. 2, where Romantic warmth emerges beneath a boldly pared-down style. As a prelude, Emilie Mayer’s Overture no. 2 acts as a bridge: a confident Romantic voice, a German link between French and Finnish colors, already projecting toward the future.</p>\n<div style=\"background-color: #f8f4ff; border: 2px solid #7d50b3; padding: 25px; margin: 20px 0; border-radius: 0px; color: #2c2c2c; line-height: 1.6; box-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.05); width: 100%;\"><strong><em>POETIC</em> MUSICAL TAG: </strong>​<br />\nA great classic of the repertoire that takes you on an emotional journey.</div>\n<p><em><a href=\"https://www.osm.ca/en/mystery-ticket/\">Mystery Tickets</a></em> (surprise seats between $28 and $30) are available for this concert! Click on “Buy tickets” and enter the promo code <strong>MYST</strong> to purchase them.</p>\n"
      }
    ]
  },
