      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Payare Conducts Berlioz and Beethoven"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>Beethoven’s masterful Piano Concerto no. 1 adheres to the rules of the Classical style, yet its lighthearted score, interspersed with inflections that foreshadow later works, announces the composer’s highly personal style. Since its premiere, Berlioz’s <em>Symphonie fantastiqu</em>e has continued to elicit enthusiasm from audiences. Its originality, along with its colourful and potent orchestration, have elevated it to the status of an icon of the symphonic repertoire.</p>\n"
      }
    ]
  },
