    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>A concert is always a quest: a search for an ideal light born from the intense encounter between artists who come together for only a few rehearsals. This same search for light runs through the entire program. In <em>Elysium</em>, premiered in 2021, Samy Moussa explores an inner, spiritual radiance inspired by the sacred realm of Greek mythology, a place of peace and transcendence. In contrast, Stravinsky’s <em>The Firebird</em>, first performed in Paris in 1910 by the Ballets Russes, ignites light from the shimmering feathers of its legendary, fiery creature. All of it unfolds in a blazing orchestral display under the direction of Rafael Payare.</p>\n<div style=\"background-color: #f8f4ff; border: 2px solid #7d50b3; padding: 25px; margin: 20px 0; border-radius: 0px; color: #2c2c2c; line-height: 1.6; box-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.05); width: 100%;\"><strong><em>EXPRESS</em> MUSICAL TAG: </strong>​<br />\nClassical concert presented without intermission, in a relaxed and welcoming atmosphere!</div>\n<p><em><a href=\"https://www.osm.ca/en/mystery-ticket/\">Mystery Tickets</a></em> (surprise seats between $28 and $30) are available for this concert! Click on “Buy tickets” and enter the promo code <strong>MYST</strong> to purchase them.</p>\n"
      }
    ]
