    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>Balancing metaphysical reflection with flashes of whimsy, this program reveals the full dramatic range of Strauss.<em> Death and Transfiguration </em>elevates the evening with a poignant musical fresco in which a soul, standing at the threshold of death, finds peace in the light. With <em>Till Eulenspiegel</em>, the mood shifts entirely: sharp strokes, leaping rhythms, and irresistible orchestral humor. Then comes<em> Don Quixote,</em> whose variations take on a rare expressive intensity thanks to Alisa Weilerstein’s cello, beautifully supported by Rafael Payare. An alternate version of this concert is also offered, featuring <em>Don Juan</em> in place of <em>Till Eulenspiegel</em>.</p>\n<div style=\"background-color: #f8f4ff; border: 2px solid #7d50b3; padding: 25px; margin: 20px 0; border-radius: 0px; color: #2c2c2c; line-height: 1.6; box-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.05); width: 100%;\"><strong><em>GRANDIOSE</em> MUSICAL TAG: </strong>​<br />\nA large-scale masterpiece where the full power of the orchestra delivers a truly breathtaking experience.</div>\n<p><em><a href=\"https://www.osm.ca/en/mystery-ticket/\">Mystery Tickets</a></em> (surprise seats between $28 and $30) are available for this concert! Click on “Buy tickets” and enter the promo code <strong>MYST</strong> to purchase them.</p>\n"
