    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Experience the Orchestra’s power in the world premieres of the 2026 Azrieli Music Prizes laureates. The program spans themes from sacrifice in Nazi-occupied Poland to a centuries-old riddle, the legacy of Occitan trobairitz, and evocative Canadian landscapes. With soloists on viola da gamba, theremin and cello, this concert offers a unique musical journey. Created in 2014, the Azrieli Music Prizes are now among Canada’s major composition competitions."
      }
