        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>Haydn played a key role in the evolution of the string quartet, and his final <em>Quartet Op. 77  No. 2</em> is full of subtle experimentation that is both inventive and elegant. Meanwhile, Shostakovich reinterprets classical forms in his <em>Quintet</em>, infusing it with his deeply personal language and profound emotional intensity.</p>\n"
