      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>By adding a second cello instead of the traditional second viola to his <em>String  Quintet</em>, Schubert redefined the boundaries of chamber music, giving his work an almost orchestral depth. The timeless <em>Adagio</em> is a pinnacle of expressiveness.</p>\n"
      }
    ]
  },
