    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Steeped in the myths that inspire it, this program radiates solar energy. The Firebird spreads its legendary wings—a blazing figure of rebirth and enchantment—in a sweeping orchestral fresco ignited by Stravinsky. With Elysium, Samy Moussa invokes Greco-Roman mythology to explore life’s beauty, fragility, and ethical meaning. At the heart of this triptych, Leonidas Kavakos takes on Tchaikovsky’s Violin Concerto, revealing its profound lyricism, wounded nobility, and intimate rhythmic poetry. An evening shaped by imaginary forces and vital energies that illuminate our inner world. POETIC MUSICAL TAG: ​ A great classic of the repertoire that takes you on an emotional journey. Mystery Tickets (surprise seats between $28 and $30) are available for this concert! Click on “Buy tickets” and enter the promo code MYST to purchase them."
      }
    ],
